                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n[i] Note for Oculus users: you can do a Windows 7 compatibility fix to get game working on Oculus. There's also a beta branch that has Oculus compatibility [/i]\n\nSo this is yet another free Bartending game in VR. I believe there are 2 others: Taphouse VR, some alien space bar one that was really bad and whose name I can't remember. There's also several paid ones. How does this one stack up?\n\nWell, it couldn't be worse than the alien space one. But it's not as good as Taphouse VR. In my opinion, it's probably the 2nd worst out of all the bartending games I have played. There's really not much to this game. Customers come in with a colored shirt. You match the drink color to their shirt color. You lay the beer down on the bar table and it shoots towards them. The whole process is clunky and not fun. \n\nThere really isn't anything else to the game. The graphics are subpar. The sounds also. The game is free. But just get Taphouse VR instead. Or pay for a good one.\n\nRate 4/10. I mean it is free. Some effort went into making it. Nice job for a what I assume is a first time dev. It's just not good enough to recommend, even at the free price.",
